FATAL_OBJECTIONS: [
  "N4 (prior-art, unanimous 5/5): A-RAG Context Tracker (arXiv 2602.03442 §3) verbatim 'records which chunks have been READ ... to prevent redundant information retrieval' — direct mechanism collision on the claim's narrow novelty (live-window-residency retrieval gating). Dataset-independent kill. Packet-sourced verbatim quote; corroborated by 'To Retrieve or To Think?' (2601.08747) as same-family. novelty_killer notes A-RAG is Feb-2026 and could not independently re-verify via live egress, but does NOT rest the kill solely on it — GPTCache operational equivalence (below) independently dissolves the mechanism.",
  "N1 (operational equivalence, 4/5 strong + 1/5 qualified): in-context gate vs semantic query cache at matched ~29% skip on 1,868 paired LLM-in-loop turns → F1 Δ=+0.0004, 95% CI [-0.0045,+0.0053]; precision Δ CI straddles 0 at every skip≥20%. The live-window vs past-query distinction produces zero measurable delta. HOWEVER — theory_skeptic correctly notes this equivalence may be STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED on single-doc CoQA (W≈history-length, gate and cache index the same topical manifold) rather than an empirical discovery generalizable to multi-doc long-horizon agents. This qualification is valid and affects the scope of N1 but does NOT rescue the claim: even if N1 is setup-confounded, N4 kills independently.",
  "Cheap signal collapse (supporting, not independent kill): AUC 0.570 (embedding) / 0.554 (lexical) vs oracle 1.0 — near-chance on real data. The L0's 0.84–1.00 AUC was generator-tautological (item-id seeded text). Real embedding beats lexical by only +0.016. The gate family is weak on real data."
]
