  "For any future resurrection attempt on a DIFFERENT axis: multi-document, multi-hop, long-horizon agent traces where live-window and past-query-set can structurally DIVERGE (theory_skeptic's valid point). CoQA single-doc is insufficient to prove operational death of the concept in general — only that it fails here and is pre-empted by prior art everywhere.",
  "Skip-overlap diagnostic (Jaccard of skipped-turn-sets between gate and cache) — the single most diagnostic missing statistic per theory_skeptic. Without it, F1 parity could be 'same turns skipped' (trivial) vs 'different turns, coincidentally equal' (non-trivial). This does not change the verdict but would sharpen the negative's publishable value.",
